cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these measurements or the numbers derived from them, please cite this repository."
title: "kv-cache-lab: VRAM accounting for KV cache quantization on consumer GPUs"
abstract: >-
  A single-script measurement of what KV cache quantization saves in VRAM on a consumer
  GPU. A straight-line fit across five context lengths gives 32.11 +/- 1.24 KiB/token for
  f16 and 19.08 +/- 1.05 for q8_0 on an RTX 4060 Laptop with Qwen2.5-1.5B - but the
  residuals reject that model (F = 2748 against a 5% critical value of 18.513). Adding a
  one-time 67.1 MiB allocation step at context 8192 fits the same data to within 1 MiB and
  moves the slopes to 29.99 and 17.31 KiB/token. The per-token overhead over theory is
  therefore about 2.0 KiB rather than the 4.1 KiB a naive fit reports; half of the
  difference is the allocation step annualised over 32K tokens. The repository ships the
  measuring script, the raw CSVs, and 72 self-checks that recompute every quoted number
  without a GPU. A quadratic fit, which carries the same three parameters as the step model, is rejected by a factor of 486 on f16 and 6.6 on q8_0, so the bend is a jump rather than curvature.
